{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99890","id":2208629180,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6DpQG8","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99890","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99890.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99890.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99890","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99890/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/99890/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99890/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/8e00035f086c62558d03217a1f4c03594618344e","number":99890,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Introduce `Viewport` functions for keeping the mouse over state consistent","user":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauermann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- resolve #89757\r\n- resolve #98003\r\n- resolve parts of #97267\r\n- resolve duplicate #90413\r\n- supersedes #89868\r\n- supersedes #90444\r\n- usage demo https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/pull/1142\r\n\r\nSome users had problems with forwarding input events to `SubViewport` since #88992, which adjusted a default value and in effect prevented calling `gui_input` when used without changes.\r\nI still believe, that this change makes mouse-handling more consistent. But this change makes it necessary to give users tools and instructions about how to deal with this new situation.\r\nPreviously I did believe, that sending `NOTIFICATION_VP_MOUSE_ENTER` and `NOTIFICATION_VP_MOUSE_EXIT` was sufficient (see https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/pull/1139), but the MRP of #98003 demonstrates, that this approach still leaves some situations unresolved.\r\n\r\nSo I want to introduce with this PR two functions, that allow users to notify viewports about the mouse-over state. These two functions take care of all internal state-adjustments.\r\n\r\nI discarded #90444 as a solution, because while it automatically handles the mouse-enter-part, users still have no solution for the mouse-exit-part.\r\nI discarded #89868 as a solution, because it is restricted to `TextureRect` and doesn't provide a generic solution for all potential relevant nodes.\r\n\r\nThe introduction of these two function with their descriptions could be seen as either a partial or a total fix of issue #97267. \r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https:/